# CroxShare environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# On Render, set these in the dashboard (Environment tab) instead of committing them.
# NOTE: none of these are strictly required to run the app.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Handled automatically — you normally do NOT set these yourself:
#   PORT      -> Render (and most hosts) inject this; server.js reads it.
#   NODE_ENV  -> set to "production" by the `npm start` script.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: TURN server for WebRTC NAT traversal.
# Without these, the app falls back to public STUN, which works for most
# LAN / simple-NAT cases. Add them only if some peers fail to connect
# (e.g. on strict mobile/corporate networks). Get them from a TURN provider
# such as Metered, Twilio, or a self-hosted coturn instance.
# TURN_URLS accepts a comma-separated list.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TURN_URLS=turn:your-turn-host:3478,turns:your-turn-host:5349
# TURN_USERNAME=your-username
# TURN_CREDENTIAL=your-password
